            {
              "feedback": {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "strong": true,
                        "text": "1. Activation Energy."
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " The graph shows that the energy of the transition state is higher than that of the reactants A and B by an amount equal to "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "E"
                      },
                      {
                        "sub": true,
                        "text": "a"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ", the activation energy. Thus, the sum of the kinetic energies of A and B must be equal to or greater than "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "E"
                      },
                      {
                        "sub": true,
                        "text": "a"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " to reach the transition state. Click on 2, the transition state, next."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "e52d57a697364b1183a6709b31ff7b3a",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "2619189173"
              },
              "id": "239901358",
              "legacyMatch": "e0010676f2a04f89a04567d769a88f7c",
              "rule": "input like {e0010676f2a04f89a04567d769a88f7c}",
              "score": 1
            },
            {
              "feedback": {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "strong": true,
                        "text": "2. Transition State."
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " After the transition state is reached, and as C and D begin to form, the system loses energy until its total energy is lower than that of the initial mixture. This lost energy is transferred to other molecules, giving them enough energy to reach the transition state. The forward reaction (between molecules A and B) therefore tends to take place readily once the reaction has started. Click on 3, change in enthalpy, Δ"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "H"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ", next."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "fc47b72bcc5c4043b9771310e91509c4",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "3979260627"
              },
              "id": "1577014174",
              "legacyMatch": "ee8281b4caeb4a71ab046eda2c3af4d0",
              "rule": "input like {ee8281b4caeb4a71ab046eda2c3af4d0}",
              "score": 1
            },
            {
              "feedback": {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "strong": true,
                        "text": "3. Change in Enthalpy."
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " Δ"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "H"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " represents the difference in enthalpy between the reactants (A and B) and the products (C and D). Click on 4, activation energy + change in enthalpy, next. "
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "da801380b180418db61cc6bc057124cf",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "2544307586"
              },
              "id": "3150356532",
              "legacyMatch": "fe25bf29510044d1930cc6bdf610db58",
              "rule": "input like {fe25bf29510044d1930cc6bdf610db58}",
              "score": 1
            },
            {
              "feedback": {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "strong": true,
                        "text": "4. Activation Energy + Change in Enthalpy."
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " The sum of "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "E"
                      },
                      {
                        "sub": true,
                        "text": "a"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " and Δ"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "H"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " represents the activation energy for the reverse reaction:  C + D ⟶ A + B"
